---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import brandingImg from "../assets/general/branding-costs.jpg";
import CTABanner from "../components/CTABanner.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <!-- Hero Article Header (no author, date, or read time as requested) -->
  <article class="bg-brand-navy text-white pt-20 pb-20 px-8">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto flex flex-col items-start">
      <h1
        class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl font-heading mb-8 font-semibold leading-[1.1] text-brand-green"
      >
        How Much Does Branding Cost in the UK? (2026 Guide)
      </h1>

      <p class="hero-subtext mb-12 max-w-3xl">
        Branding in the UK typically costs between £1,500 and £50,000+,
        depending on scope and agency experience. Here's an honest breakdown of
        what to expect at every budget level — from a Bristol agency with 25
        years' experience.
      </p>

      <!-- Featured Image -->
      <div class="w-full mb-16 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl">
        <Image
          src={brandingImg}
          alt="Branding Cost and Identity Guidelines Kit"
          class="w-full h-auto object-cover max-h-[500px]"
        />
      </div>

      <!-- Quick Answer: Blue Box (as screenshot page 10 & 12) -->
      <div
        class="w-full bg-brand-blue text-white rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-12 mb-16 shadow-xl"
      >
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mb-6 text-white">
          Quick Answer: UK Branding Costs at a Glance
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-3 font-body text-base md:text-lg mb-8 text-blue-50">
          <p>
            <strong class="text-white">Logo design only:</strong> £500 – £3,000
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-white"
              >Brand starter pack (logo + guidelines):</strong
            > £1,500 – £5,000
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-white">Full brand identity:</strong> £5,000 – £20,000
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-white">Complete rebrand with strategy:</strong> £10,000
            – £50,000+
          </p>
        </div>
        <div
          class="pt-6 border-t border-blue-400/40 text-sm md:text-base text-blue-100 font-light space-y-1 mb-6"
        >
          <p>
            <strong class="text-white font-medium">Budget rule of thumb:</strong
            > 10-15% of projected annual revenue for a full rebrand
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-white font-medium">Typical timescale:</strong> 4-10
            weeks for a full brand project
          </p>
        </div>
        <a
          href="/services"
          class="inline-block text-white underline font-semibold hover:text-brand-green transition-colors text-base"
        >
          See all our services
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Content Sections (Screenshots from pages 12 and 13) -->
      <div class="space-y-16 text-white font-body w-full">
        <!-- What's Typically Included -->
        <div
          class="bg-[#121c32] border border-gray-800 rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-10"
        >
          <h2
            class="font-heading text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-brand-green mb-4"
          >
            What's Typically Included in a Branding Package?
          </h2>
          <p
            class="text-gray-200 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed font-light"
          >
            The deliverables vary by package, but a well-structured brand
            project should typically include: Brand strategy (positioning
            statement, audience definition, messaging framework, tone of voice),
            Visual identity (logo and variations, colour palette, typography,
            photography style), Brand guidelines document covering usage rules
            and application examples, Brand assets including stationery, email
            signature, social media templates, and presentation templates.
            Always clarify the scope in writing before work begins.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- How to Budget for a Branding Project -->
        <div
          class="bg-[#121c32] border border-gray-800 rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-10 space-y-8"
        >
          <h2
            class="font-heading text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-brand-green"
          >
            How to Budget for a Branding Project
          </h2>

          <div>
            <h3 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">
              The 10-15% rule
            </h3>
            <p
              class="text-gray-200 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed font-light"
            >
              For businesses undertaking a full rebrand, allocating 10-15% of
              your projected annual revenue is a useful starting point. For a
              business turning over £200,000 a year, that suggests a branding
              budget of £20,000–£30,000 — enough to do the job properly with a
              mid-tier specialist agency.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">
              Prioritise strategy before design
            </h3>
            <p
              class="text-gray-200 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed font-light"
            >
              The most expensive branding mistake is investing in design before
              you're clear on strategy. If your positioning is wrong, the best
              logo in the world won't fix it. If budget is tight, consider a
              strategy workshop first, then phase the design work when you're
              ready.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">
              Factor in rollout costs
            </h3>
            <p
              class="text-gray-200 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed font-light"
            >
              Once the identity is created, you'll need to update your website,
              printed materials, signage, email templates, and social profiles.
              Build this into your overall budget — the design is often only
              40-60% of the total investment.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Is Branding Worth the Investment? -->
        <div
          class="bg-[#121c32] border border-gray-800 rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-10"
        >
          <h2
            class="font-heading text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-brand-green mb-4"
          >
            Is Branding Worth the Investment?
          </h2>
          <p
            class="text-gray-200 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed font-light"
          >
            A well-executed brand identity is one of the highest-ROI investments
            a growing business can make. It allows you to charge more —
            businesses with strong brands are perceived as more professional and
            trustworthy, which directly supports higher pricing. It attracts
            better clients by acting as a filter for the right fit. It reduces
            marketing friction by ensuring every piece of content reinforces the
            same message. At Bob Design, we've seen clients increase their
            average project value by 40% following a rebrand.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Frequently Asked Questions -->
        <div
          class="bg-[#121c32] border border-gray-800 rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-10 space-y-6"
        >
          <h2
            class="font-heading text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-brand-green"
          >
            Frequently Asked Questions
          </h2>

          <div>
            <h3 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">
              How much does branding cost for a small business in the UK?
            </h3>
            <p
              class="text-gray-200 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed font-light"
            >
              For a small business in the UK, budget at least £1,500–£5,000 for
              a professional brand starter pack. A full brand identity with
              strategy typically starts from £5,000–£10,000 with a specialist
              agency. Freelancer rates are available from around £500–£2,000,
              but the level of strategic thinking and creative quality will vary
              significantly.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
